---
// F5 and F7, the mission of Ch. 6: from a random start, after a while every node the same colour. F5: a funnel of
// numbers, all 262 144 rules, the 512 that are their own cousin (either colour may win) and the 27 whose average next
// density moves away from half and half, found without a simulation; then all 27 race on one rewired grid from one start
// (the network and start of F7), within the thesis's 100 rounds: a few agree, the simple threshold rule is stuck. F7:
// the winner at work on that grid, the threshold rule on the same start, and twenty fresh networks. Data:
// src/data/defence/consensus.json (scripts/defence/precompute.ts); the run and its verdict: src/scripts/defence/agree.ts.
import Slide from './Slide.astro';
import SimButton from './SimButton.astro';
import { texify, phi } from './tex';
---
<Slide id="ch-synchronisation" label="Can the rule predict the behaviour?" builds={4} class="f5" ch={6}>
  <h2>Can the rule predict the behaviour?</h2>
  <p class="lede">The mission: after a while, all nodes the same colour.</p>
  <div class="row grow f5-row">
    <div class="funnel">
      <div class="tier" data-b="1"><b>262&#8239;144</b><span>every rule</span></div>
      <div class="tier" data-b="2"><b>512</b><span>treat on and off alike</span></div>
      <div class="tier last" data-b="3"><b>27</b><span>move away from half and half</span></div>
      <p class="nosim" data-b="3">without a single simulation</p>
    </div>
    <div class="race" data-b="3">
      <p class="race-head">The 27, run from the same start</p>
      <div class="race-box">
        <canvas class="tiles" aria-label="The 27 rules, each on the same rewired grid of 900 nodes from the same start"></canvas>
        <SimButton class="f5-btn" />
      </div>
      <p class="race-key"><span class="key thr">simple threshold</span><span class="key win">the winner</span><b data-count></b></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p slot="say">Can we really use what a rule looks like to predict what it will do? A test, in the form of a mission: from a random start, after a while every node should have the same colour, all on or all off. The obvious candidates are threshold rules: do what most of your neighbours do. On a network they get stuck, in patches that each agree with themselves but never with each other.</p>
  <p slot="say" set:html={texify('There are 262 144 rules at resolution 9. First filter: we do not care which colour wins, only that both are equally likely, so the rule must treat on and off alike: it must be its own cousin. That leaves 512. Second filter, on the average next density: from half on and half off, the network must move away, towards all on or all off. That leaves 27, about one rule in ten thousand, found in a fraction of a second without a single simulation.')} />
  <p slot="say" set:html={texify('Now we can afford to run every one of them. Here all 27 run on the same grid of 900 nodes, a fifth of its links rewired, from the same random start, for at most 100 rounds, as in the thesis. Most of them freeze in patches within a few rounds, or keep churning, and fade; the simple threshold rule is stuck from round 10. Three reach agreement. Run over hundreds of networks, one of them is clearly the best: $\phi^9_{488,464}$, which brought more than 96% of the rewired grids of the thesis to agreement. It is among the most sensitive of the 27, but sensitivity alone is not enough: the filter narrows the search down, and only a run decides (Chapter 6, Physica D 2025).')} />
</Slide>

<Slide label="Watch it work" builds={3} class="f7" ch={6}>
  <div class="row grow f7-row">
    <div class="f7-box">
      <canvas class="grid" aria-label="The chosen rule on a rewired 30 by 30 grid"></canvas>
      <SimButton class="f7-btn" />
    </div>
    <div class="col f7-side">
      <h2>Watch it work</h2>
      <div class="f7-rules" role="group" aria-label="Rule">
        <button type="button" class="ctl" data-rule="winner" aria-pressed="true">The winner <span set:html={phi(9, 488, 464)} /></button>
        <button type="button" class="ctl" data-rule="threshold" aria-pressed="false">Simple threshold <span set:html={phi(9, 480, 496)} /></button>
      </div>
      <canvas class="trace" aria-label="Share of nodes on, round by round"></canvas>
      <div class="trials" data-b="2">
        <p><span data-won>0</span> of 20 fresh networks agreed</p>
        <div class="dots" data-dots>{Array.from({ length: 20 }, () => <i />)}<SimButton class="f7-btn2" /></div>
      </div>
      <p class="result" data-b="3"><b>Our result</b> 27 candidates out of 262 144, without a single simulation. The best one brings most networks to agreement.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p slot="say">The winner at work, on the grid of the race (900 nodes, eight neighbours each, a fifth of the links rewired), from the same random start with half of the nodes on. Patches form and fight, and from round 31 every node is on. The curve on the right is the share of nodes that are on, round by round.</p>
  <p slot="say">The buttons switch to the simple threshold rule, on the same network from the same start: within a dozen rounds it freezes into patches, each content with its own majority, a few nodes blinking at the borders. Then twenty fresh networks, each with its own start, for whichever rule is chosen: the winner brings 19 of the 20 to agreement, the threshold rule none. These grids are a small illustration; the thesis ran 900 samples for every setting, on rewired rings, rewired grids and scale-free networks.</p>
</Slide>

<style>
  .f5-row { gap: calc(64 * var(--u)); align-items: flex-start; }
  .funnel { width: calc(640 * var(--u)); flex: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
  .tier { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; padding: calc(12 * var(--u)) calc(20 * var(--u)); border: calc(3 * var(--u)) solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); position: relative; }
  .tier:nth-child(1) { width: 100%; }
  .tier:nth-child(2) { width: 88%; }
  .tier:nth-child(3) { width: 78%; }
  .tier b { font-size: calc(68 * var(--u)); line-height: 1.05; }
  .tier span { font-size: calc(30 * var(--u)); color: var(--muted); text-align: center; white-space: nowrap; }
  .tier + .tier { margin-top: calc(40 * var(--u)); }
  /* the funnel narrows: an arrow down into each tier */
  .tier + .tier::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: calc(-36 * var(--u)); left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); border: calc(15 * var(--u)) solid transparent; border-top-color: var(--accent); }
  .tier.last { background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--sun); }
  .tier.last span { color: var(--sun); opacity: 0.85; }
  .nosim { font-size: calc(38 * var(--u)); font-weight: 700; margin-top: calc(24 * var(--u)); }
  .race { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(12 * var(--u)); }
  .race-head { font-size: calc(34 * var(--u)); color: var(--muted); }
  .race-box { position: relative; }
  .tiles { width: calc(1010 * var(--u)); height: calc(584 * var(--u)); }
  .race-box :global(.f5-btn) { right: calc(-6 * var(--u)); bottom: calc(10 * var(--u)); }
  .race-key { font-size: calc(32 * var(--u)); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: calc(36 * var(--u)); }
  .key { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: calc(12 * var(--u)); }
  .key::before { content: ''; width: calc(26 * var(--u)); height: calc(26 * var(--u)); border: calc(4 * var(--u)) solid var(--ink); }
  .key.win::before { border-color: var(--danger); border-width: calc(5 * var(--u)); }
  .key.win { color: var(--danger); font-weight: 700; }
  [data-count] { margin-left: auto; font-size: calc(40 * var(--u)); }
  .key.win, [data-count] { transition: opacity 0.4s ease; }
  :global(.f5:not(.raced)) .key.win, :global(.f5:not(.raced)) [data-count] { opacity: 0; }

  .f7-row { gap: calc(60 * var(--u)); align-items: center; }
  .f7-box { position: relative; flex: none; }
  :global(.f7) .grid { width: calc(780 * var(--u)); height: calc(780 * var(--u)); }
  .f7-box :global(.f7-btn) { right: calc(-32 * var(--u)); bottom: calc(-24 * var(--u)); }
  .f7-side { gap: calc(24 * var(--u)); flex: 1; }
  .f7-rules { display: flex; gap: calc(14 * var(--u)); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .f7-rules .ctl { font-size: calc(30 * var(--u)); padding: calc(8 * var(--u)) calc(20 * var(--u)); }
  .f7-rules .ctl[aria-pressed="true"] { background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--sun); }
  .trace { width: 100%; height: calc(260 * var(--u)); }
  .trials p { font-size: calc(34 * var(--u)); }
  .dots { display: flex; gap: calc(10 * var(--u)); margin-top: calc(10 * var(--u)); position: relative; align-items: center; }
  .dots :global(.f7-btn2) { position: relative; margin-left: calc(20 * var(--u)); }
  .dots i { width: calc(34 * var(--u)); height: calc(34 * var(--u)); border-radius: 50%; border: calc(3 * var(--u)) solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); }
  .dots i.ok { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .dots i.no { background: var(--panel); border-color: var(--muted); }
  .dots i.run { border-color: var(--accent); }
  :global(.f7) .result { font-size: calc(34 * var(--u)); }
</style>

<script>
  import { slide, sim, buildOf } from '../../scripts/defence/deck';
  import { stage, onSize, ticker } from '../../scripts/defence/stage';
  import { axes, curve, label, px, py, type Plot } from '../../scripts/defence/plot';
  import { makeRng, lattice } from '../../scripts/net';
  import { type Rule, randomState, density } from '../../scripts/llna';
  import { agreement, WINNER, THRESHOLD, type Agreement, type Outcome } from '../../scripts/defence/agree';
  import { parse } from '../../scripts/palette';
  import data from '../../data/defence/consensus.json';

  const cands = data.candidates as { B: number; S: number; bs8: number; slope: number }[];
  const is = (c: { B: number; S: number }, r: Rule) => c.B === r.B && c.S === r.S;
  // the rewired grid of the mission (eight neighbours each, a fifth of the links rewired) and the start, for F5 and F7
  const SIDE = 30, P_REWIRE = 0.2, demo = data.demo;
  const demoNet = () => lattice(SIDE, 8, P_REWIRE, makeRng(demo.netSeed)), demoStart = () => randomState(SIDE * SIDE, 0.5, makeRng(demo.startSeed));

  // ── F5: a funnel of numbers; then the 27 race on the same grid from the same start, ten rounds a second, for at most
  // the thesis's 100 rounds. A tile that reaches agreement is framed; one that freezes or is still churning at the end
  // fades. The simple threshold rule is ringed from the start, the winner once the race is over. The start is fixed:
  // the speaker text quotes the outcome, and F7 replays two of the tiles. ──
  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.f5')) {
    const c = s.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas.tiles')!, count = s.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-count]')!;
    const COLS = 7, GAP = 22, PAD = 12, LIMIT = 100;
    const net = demoNet(), first = demoStart();
    let runs: Agreement[] = [], verdict: (Outcome | null)[] = [];
    // one 30 × 30 bitmap per tile, scaled up without smoothing: square cells
    const bits = cands.map(() => { const o = document.createElement('canvas'); o.width = o.height = SIDE; return o; });
    const over = () => {
      const done = verdict.every(Boolean);
      s.classList.toggle('raced', done);
      count.textContent = done ? `${verdict.filter((v) => v!.ok).length} of 27 agree` : '';
    };
    const reset = () => { runs = cands.map((r) => agreement(net, { r: 9, B: r.B, S: r.S }, first, LIMIT)); verdict = runs.map(() => null); over(); };
    function paint() {
      const st = stage(c); if (!st) return;
      const { ctx, t } = st, T = (st.w - 2 * PAD - (COLS - 1) * GAP) / COLS;
      const on = parse(t.ink), off = parse(t.panel), done = verdict.every(Boolean);
      ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;
      cands.forEach((r, i) => {
        const x = PAD + (i % COLS) * (T + GAP), y = PAD + Math.floor(i / COLS) * (T + GAP), v = verdict[i], a = runs[i].state;
        const o = bits[i], octx = o.getContext('2d')!, img = octx.createImageData(SIDE, SIDE);
        for (let k = 0; k < a.length; k++) { const col = a[k] ? on : off; img.data[4 * k] = col[0]; img.data[4 * k + 1] = col[1]; img.data[4 * k + 2] = col[2]; img.data[4 * k + 3] = 255; }
        octx.putImageData(img, 0, 0);
        ctx.globalAlpha = v && !v.ok ? 0.22 : 1;
        ctx.drawImage(o, x, y, T, T);
        ctx.strokeStyle = t.line; ctx.lineWidth = 1.5; ctx.strokeRect(x, y, T, T);
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
        if (v?.ok) { ctx.strokeStyle = t.accent; ctx.lineWidth = 6; ctx.strokeRect(x - 3, y - 3, T + 6, T + 6); }
        if (is(r, THRESHOLD)) { ctx.strokeStyle = t.ink; ctx.lineWidth = 4; ctx.strokeRect(x - 8, y - 8, T + 16, T + 16); }
        if (is(r, WINNER) && done) { ctx.strokeStyle = t.danger; ctx.lineWidth = 5; ctx.strokeRect(x - 8, y - 8, T + 16, T + 16); }
      });
    }
    const race = ticker(s, 10, () => {
      runs.forEach((r, i) => { if (!verdict[i]) verdict[i] = r.next(); });
      const done = verdict.every(Boolean);
      if (done) over();
      return done;
    }, paint);
    sim(s.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-simbtn]')!, 4, { reset() { race.play(false); reset(); paint(); }, play() { race.play(true); } });
    slide(s, { leave() { race.play(false); } });
    reset();
    onSize(c, paint);
  }

  // ── F7: the winner (or the threshold rule) on a rewired grid; then twenty fresh networks ──
  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.f7')) {
    const [grid, trace] = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas'));
    const side = SIDE, N = side * side, p = P_REWIRE;
    const net = demoNet(), first = demoStart();
    const RULES: Record<string, Rule> = { winner: WINNER, threshold: THRESHOLD };
    const buttons = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-rule]'));
    let pick = 'winner', run: Agreement, rho: number[] = [], end: { ok: boolean; tick: number } | null = null;
    const reset = () => { run = agreement(net, RULES[pick], first); rho = [density(first)]; end = null; };
    function paintGrid() {
      const st = stage(grid); if (!st) return;
      const { ctx, t } = st, cell = st.w / side, a = run.state;
      ctx.fillStyle = t.panel; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, st.w, st.h); ctx.fillStyle = t.ink;
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) if (a[i]) ctx.fillRect((i % side) * cell, Math.floor(i / side) * cell, cell - 1.5, cell - 1.5);
    }
    function paintTrace() {
      const st = stage(trace); if (!st) return;
      const { t } = st, T = Math.max(60, rho.length), q: Plot = { x: 150, y: 10, w: st.w - 170, h: st.h - 100, x0: 0, x1: T, y0: 0, y1: 1 };
      axes(st, q, { xticks: [[0, '0'], [T, String(T)]], yticks: [[0, '0'], [1, '1']], xname: 'round', yname: 'share on' });
      curve(st, q, () => 0.5, t.line, 2, [6, 8]);
      st.ctx.strokeStyle = t.accent; st.ctx.lineWidth = 3; st.ctx.beginPath();
      rho.forEach((v, i) => { const X = px(q, i), Y = py(q, v); if (i) st.ctx.lineTo(X, Y); else st.ctx.moveTo(X, Y); });
      st.ctx.stroke();
      if (end) label(st, end.ok ? `all the same from round ${end.tick}` : `stuck from round ${end.tick}`, st.w - 10, 24, { size: 28, align: 'right', color: end.ok ? t.accent : t.danger, weight: 600, bg: true });
    }
    // three rounds a second; it stops when the verdict is in
    const ticks = ticker(s, 3, () => {
      if (end) return true;
      end = run.next(); rho.push(density(run.state));
      return !!end;
    }, () => { paintGrid(); paintTrace(); });
    // twenty trials of the chosen rule, a slice of rounds per frame so no frame waits
    const dots = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-dots] i')), won = s.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-won]')!;
    let job = 0;
    const clear = () => { cancelAnimationFrame(job); job = 0; dots.forEach((d) => d.className = ''); won.textContent = '0'; };
    function trials() {
      clear();
      const rule = RULES[pick], seeds = data.trials.winner;
      let i = 0, wins = 0, tr: Agreement;
      const begin = () => { const x = seeds[i]; tr = agreement(lattice(side, 8, p, makeRng(x.netSeed)), rule, randomState(N, 0.5, makeRng(x.startSeed))); dots[i].className = 'run'; };
      begin();
      const frame = () => {
        const t0 = performance.now();
        while (performance.now() - t0 < 4 && i < 20) {
          const v = tr.next();
          if (v) { dots[i].className = v.ok ? 'ok' : 'no'; if (v.ok) wins++; won.textContent = String(wins); i++; if (i < 20) begin(); }
        }
        if (i < 20) job = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      };
      job = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }
    const mark = () => buttons.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.rule === pick)));
    // another rule: back to the same start, and what ran runs on; once the trials are up, they run again for it
    buttons.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (b.dataset.rule === pick) return;
      pick = b.dataset.rule!; mark();
      const going = ticks.playing; ticks.play(false); reset(); paintGrid(); paintTrace();
      if (going) ticks.play(true);
      if (buildOf(s) >= 2) trials(); else clear();
    }));
    reset();
    const [gridBtn, trialBtn] = s.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-simbtn]');
    sim(gridBtn, 1, { reset() { ticks.play(false); reset(); paintGrid(); paintTrace(); }, play() { ticks.play(true); } });
    sim(trialBtn, 2, { reset: clear, play: trials });
    slide(s, { enter() { pick = 'winner'; mark(); reset(); clear(); }, leave() { ticks.play(false); cancelAnimationFrame(job); } });
    onSize(grid, paintGrid); onSize(trace, paintTrace);
  }
</script>
